Here's a step-by-step guide on how to create a Capacitor plugin to expose the OneWelcome iOS SDK to your React micro frontends and interact with the `authenticateUserWith` method.

**Step 1: Create a new Capacitor plugin**

Open your terminal and run the following command to create a new Capacitor plugin:
```bash
npx @capacitor/cli create-plugin my-plugin
```
This will create a new directory called `my-plugin` with the basic structure for a Capacitor plugin.

**Step 2: Install the required dependencies**

In the `my-plugin` directory, install the required dependencies:
```bash
npm install @one-welcome/ios-sdk
```
This will install the OneWelcome iOS SDK.

**Step 3: Create the plugin interface**

In the `my-plugin` directory, create a new file called `index.ts`. This file will contain the plugin interface:
```typescript
import { Plugin, PluginConfig } from '@capacitor/core';
import { OneWelcome } from '@one-welcome/ios-sdk';

export interface OneWelcomePlugin extends Plugin {
  authenticateUserWith: (options: {
    userProfile: string;
    authenticator: string;
    delegate: any;
  }) => Promise<void>;
}

export class OneWelcomePluginImpl implements OneWelcomePlugin {
  async authenticateUserWith(options: {
    userProfile: string;
    authenticator: string;
    delegate: any;
  }): Promise<void> {
    // Implementation will go here
  }
}
```
This interface defines the `authenticateUserWith` method, which takes three parameters: `userProfile`, `authenticator`, and `delegate`.

**Step 4: Implement the plugin**

In the `my-plugin` directory, create a new file called `impl.ts`. This file will contain the implementation of the plugin:
```typescript
import { OneWelcomePluginImpl } from './index';

class AuthenticationDelegate {
  userClient(_: any, didStartAuthenticationForUser: any, authenticator: any) {
    console.log('Authentication started');
  }

  userClient(_: any, didReceivePinChallenge: any) {
    console.log('PIN challenge received');
  }

  userClient(_: any, didReceiveBiometricChallenge: any) {
    console.log('Biometric challenge received');
  }

  userClient(_: any, didReceiveCustomAuthFinishAuthenticationChallenge: any) {
    console.log('Custom authentication challenge received');
  }

  userClient(_: any, didAuthenticateUser: any, authenticator: any, info: any) {
    console.log('User authenticated successfully');
  }

  userClient(_: any, didFailToAuthenticateUser: any, authenticator: any, error: any) {
    console.log('Authentication failed');
  }
}

export class OneWelcomePluginImpl {
  async authenticateUserWith(options: {
    userProfile: string;
    authenticator: string;
    delegate: any;
  }): Promise<void> {
    const userClient = OneWelcome.SharedUserClient.instance;
    const authenticator = OneWelcome.AuthenticatorFactory.createAuthenticator(options.authenticator);
    const delegate = new AuthenticationDelegate();

    userClient.authenticateUserWith(
      options.userProfile,
      authenticator,
      delegate
    );

    // Emit events to the frontend
    this.emit('userClient:didStartAuthenticationForUser', options.userProfile, authenticator);
    this.emit('userClient:didReceivePinChallenge');
    this.emit('userClient:didReceiveBiometricChallenge');
    this.emit('userClient:didReceiveCustomAuthFinishAuthenticationChallenge');
    this.emit('userClient:didAuthenticateUser', options.userProfile, authenticator);
    this.emit('userClient:didFailToAuthenticateUser', options.userProfile, authenticator);
  }
}
```

