**Fixed Supply ERC721 NFT Collection in Solidity**
=====================================================

Below is an example of a basic ERC721 NFT collection with a fixed supply in Solidity. This contract uses the OpenZeppelin's ERC721A library for a more gas-efficient implementation.

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

import "https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/v4.4.2/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol";
import "https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/v4.4.2/contracts/token/ERC721/extensions/ERC721URIStorage.sol";
import "https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts/blob/v4.4.2/contracts/utils/Counters.sol";

contract MyNFTCollection is ERC721URIStorage {
    using Counters for Counters.Counter;
    Counters.Counter private _tokenIds;

    // Mapping of token IDs to their owners
    mapping (uint256 => address) public tokenOwners;

    // Mapping of token IDs to their metadata
    mapping (uint256 => string) public tokenMetadata;

    // Maximum supply of NFTs
    uint256 public constant MAX_SUPPLY = 1000;

    constructor() ERC721("My NFT Collection", "MNC") {
        // Initialize the token ID counter
        _tokenIds.increment();
    }

    // Function to mint a new NFT
    function mintNFT(address _to, string memory _tokenURI) public {
        // Check if the maximum supply has been reached
        require(_tokenIds.current() <= MAX_SUPPLY, "Maximum supply reached");

        // Get the current token ID
        uint256 _tokenId = _tokenIds.current();

        // Increment the token ID counter
        _tokenIds.increment();

        // Set the owner of the new NFT
        _setTokenURI(_tokenId, _tokenURI);
        _mint(_to, _tokenId);

        // Store the token metadata
        tokenMetadata[_tokenId] = _tokenURI;

        // Store the token owner
        tokenOwners[_tokenId] = _to;
    }

    // Function to get the token metadata
    function getTokenMetadata(uint256 _tokenId) public view returns (string memory) {
        return tokenMetadata[_tokenId];
    }

    // Function to get the token owner
    function getTokenOwner(uint256 _tokenId) public view returns (address) {
        return tokenOwners[_tokenId];
    }
}
```

**Explanation**

*   We import the necessary OpenZeppelin contracts for ERC721 and Counters.
*   We define a contract `MyNFTCollection` that inherits from `ERC721URIStorage`.
*   We use the `Counters` library to keep track of the token IDs.
*   We define a mapping of token IDs to their owners and metadata.
*   We set a constant `MAX_SUPPLY` to define the maximum number of NFTs that can be minted.
*   The `mintNFT` function allows users to mint a new NFT by providing the recipient's address and the
